Package: darling-platform
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Darling Platform contributors
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.39)
Description: import, manage and run macOS applications on Linux
 Darling Platform runs macOS applications on Linux on top of a pinned Darling
 release. This package provides the dg command, which inspects the host, manages
 the shared prefix where the applications live, and reports what is missing
 before anything is installed.
 .
 The package ships only that binary. Darling itself and the applications you
 import stay outside it, so removing darling-platform never deletes your prefix.
